@@ -254,3 +254,9 @@ The cart stores earlier output; Mio’s desk monitor shows only the live queue.
 The lunch counter has a single canonical price table in `game3d/js/gameplay/canteen-meals.js`. A selected meal does not debit yen until its price has been shown and the player chooses to pay. Payment records one order receipt synchronously; collection, a resumed payment checkpoint and a second visit cannot charge it again. The tray stays a local physical entitlement rather than a Bag food item. Eating records completion after the visible bites; interruption preserves the unfinished meal. Returning the tray releases the entitlement for another deliberate order.
 
 Normal departure and water use physically park a carried tray in its own counter bay. Interrupted travel has a receipt recovery fallback. Delivered and parked trays remain collectable without staff; an undelivered receipt waits for a visible worker during lunch, including after Continue in another period. A saved seated player returns to the actual chair, with the tray and action camera restored. Meals and water award no stats, bond or vocabulary. The optional dish followup uses the existing persistent heard-remark/known-word system, so either discovery order works.
+
+## Kenji outing prototype
+
+The selected [outing proposal](../../reviews/game-additions-1/review.json) has an isolated prototype with an unvoiced conversation candidate, pending story and release review. Chat with Kenji opens the optional invitation and preserves his earlier arcade topics. One travelling Kenji can follow through shotengai, plaza, east_lane, east_coast and dorm_commons. An already-met, visible and available Kenji can join on weekday evenings or weekends after early morning; scheduled club meetings take precedence. Leaving these places or changing the period pauses the walk, and a later eligible invitation can resume its completed stops.
+
+Arcade memory requires both characters to reach the existing frontage. Kenji waits outside the konbini, and shopping counts only after a new drink order is paid and collected. Coast memory requires both characters to occupy actual free adjacent bench seats. Save/Continue keeps the outing and companion pose; ending remembers the last completed stop, without awarding knowledge or relationship progress. Repeated stops repeat the physical action without another receipt. Outing side goals clear on pause or finish without clearing a replacement goal from another activity.
